---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { articles } from '../lib/data';
const targets = ['The New York Times','The Wall Street Journal','The Washington Post','Los Angeles Times','Bloomberg','Reuters','Reuters Breakingviews','Associated Press','Financial Times','The Guardian','The Verge','WIRED','TIME','Fortune','CNBC','CNN','BBC','The Information','TechCrunch','MIT Technology Review','New York Magazine','The Cut','Scientific American'];
const rows = targets.map(name => ({ name, oct: articles.filter(a => a.publication === name && a.date.startsWith('2026-10')).length, nov: articles.filter(a => a.publication === name && a.date.startsWith('2026-11')).length }));
---
<Base title="Collection coverage"><div class="page-heading"><span class="kicker">SOURCE COVERAGE / KNOWN GAPS</span><h1>Collection coverage</h1><p>Counts show publisher pages individually checked for this archive. A zero means no verified record in the file, not that an outlet published nothing.</p></div><div class="section-head"><h2>Publication × month</h2><span class="meta">01 OCT — 21 NOV 2026</span></div><div class="matrix-wrap panel"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Publication</th><th scope="col">October</th><th scope="col">November</th><th scope="col">Verified total</th><th scope="col">Collection status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{rows.map(row=><tr><th scope="row">{row.name}</th><td><span class:list={['cell',row.oct?'filled':'']}>{row.oct}</span></td><td><span class:list={['cell',row.nov?'filled':'']}>{row.nov}</span></td><td>{row.oct+row.nov}</td><td>{row.oct+row.nov?'Partial sample':'No verified record'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><section class="panel gap-note"><h2>Known gaps</h2><p>Coverage has not been demonstrated exhaustive for any outlet or month. Chinese, Japanese and other translated query sets, podcast transcripts, paywalled reports, corrections and syndicated copies need further review. Search results and feeds enter the editorial queue as leads; they do not increase public counts until an original source is checked.</p><p>Unique originals are grouped by a documented syndication key. An update to the same URL remains one article; a separately published follow-up is a new article. Current records have no confirmed syndication grouping or corrections.</p></section></Base>
<style>.matrix-wrap{overflow-x:auto}.matrix-wrap table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;min-width:650px}th,td{text-align:left;padding:13px 18px;border-bottom:1px solid #273542;font-size:13px}thead th{font:11px 'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;color:#95a9b8;letter-spacing:.07em}tbody th{font-weight:600}.cell{display:inline-flex;min-width:38px;justify-content:center;padding:6px;border-radius:4px;background:#1b2732;color:#8599a8}.cell.filled{background:#582c30;color:#ffa39b}.gap-note{padding:25px;margin-top:28px}.gap-note h2{font:600 26px 'Playfair Display',serif}.gap-note p{color:#a7b8c6;line-height:1.65;max-width:850px}</style>
